<section id="top" class="inner-hero">
        <div class="page-shell">
            <span class="eyebrow">Quickler Workflows</span>
            <h1>EICR, gas safety, van checks, site reports — over WhatsApp.</h1>
            <p>Engineers answer questions on WhatsApp. Quickler turns replies and photos into a dashboard record, flags faults, and keeps a timestamped audit trail. Per firm pricing, no per-user subscription, no app to install.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-top: 28px; justify-content: center;">
                <a href="/pages/demo.html" class="btn btn-hero-primary" data-cta="services-top-demo">Try the demo</a>
                <a href="#pricing" class="btn btn-hero-secondary" data-cta="services-top-pricing">See pricing</a>
                <a href="/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section" class="btn btn-hero-secondary" data-cta="services-top-contact">Contact</a>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top: 16px; font-size: 0.82rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4);">Jump to: <a href="#eicr" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);">EICR</a> · <a href="#cp12" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);">Gas safety</a> · <a href="#van-checks" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);">Van checks</a> · <a href="#site-reports" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);">Site inspections</a></p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="how-it-works-title">
        <div class="section-header section-header-centered">
            <div>
                <p class="section-label">How It Works</p>
                <h2 id="how-it-works-title">Four steps from site to finished document.</h2>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="balanced-grid-2">
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">1. Capture</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Capture on site</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Staff send text, voice notes, photos, and measurements to a workflow number while they are on site, not after they get back to the desk.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">2. Extract</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Sort the facts into the right structure</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">quickler reads the messages, recognises the workflow you configured, and slots the content into the correct report, record, or template structure.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">3. Review</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">The engineer stays in charge</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">The responsible person checks the draft, edits anything they want, and signs off. Nothing ships without a human eye.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">4. Output</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Finished report or admin pack</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Produce the PDF, the document, or the next workflow state. Store the evidence alongside it so the record stands up later.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="what-you-get-title">
        <div class="section-header section-header-centered">
            <div>
                <p class="section-label">What You Get</p>
                <h2 id="what-you-get-title">What you actually get.</h2>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="balanced-grid-2">
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Capture</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">WhatsApp input on site</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Staff can send text, voice notes, photos, and measurements from a tool they already use.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Structure</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Templates for each workflow</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Each workflow is shaped around the report, record, or admin pack you already produce.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Extraction</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">AI tuned to the job</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">The system pulls facts into the right structure instead of behaving like a generic chatbot.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Review</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Human sign-off stays in place</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">The accountable person reviews and edits the draft before anything is finalised.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Evidence</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Files stay with the job</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Photos, voice notes, measurements, and other files stay attached to the record they belong to.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Output</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">PDFs and finished records</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Reports and records can be produced in a format that is ready to send, file, or store.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Commercials</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Simple monthly pricing</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">One pound per report. Unlimited users and workflows. No per-engineer licence, no setup fee on standard plans.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Access</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Direct contact with the founder</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">While the product is still early, rollout and feedback stay close to the person building it.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
        <div class="section-header section-header-centered">
            <div>
                <p class="section-label">Fit</p>
                <h2 id="fit-title">Where quickler fits best.</h2>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="balanced-grid-3">
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Good fit</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Repeated workflows with a stable shape</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Inspection reports, survey summaries, maintenance visit reports, site investigation records, QA packs, approval flows, and repeated document handling.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Not ideal</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">No stable pattern</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">If every case is materially different, or review and repeated structure are barely part of the job, this is probably not the right first fit.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Strongest start</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">One real workflow, one real example</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">The best enquiries describe one workflow, how often it happens, what gets captured during the job, and what should improve.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="workflows-title">
        <div class="section-header section-header-centered">
            <div>
                <p class="section-label">Supported workflows</p>
                <h2 id="workflows-title">Compliance workflows Quickler runs over WhatsApp.</h2>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="balanced-grid-3">
            <article id="eicr" class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Electrical</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title"><a href="/pages/eicr-from-whatsapp.html">EICR — Electrical Installation Condition Report</a></h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">EICR capture on WhatsApp with photo evidence. C1, C2 and FI codes flagged on the dashboard the moment they are entered. Formatted EICR PDF for the qualifying electrician to sign off. <a href="/pages/eicr-from-whatsapp.html">Full guide →</a></p>
            </article>
            <article id="cp12" class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Gas Safe</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title"><a href="/pages/cp12-gas-safety-whatsapp.html">CP12 — Landlord Gas Safety Record</a></h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Appliance-by-appliance checks on WhatsApp with photo of each appliance plate. Formatted CP12 PDF produced for the Gas Safe registered engineer's signature. Stored against the property automatically. <a href="/pages/cp12-gas-safety-whatsapp.html">Full guide →</a></p>
            </article>
            <article id="van-checks" class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Fleet</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title"><a href="/pages/van-safety-check-template.html">Van safety checks — DVSA daily walkround</a></h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Drivers receive the walkround on WhatsApp at the start of every shift. Defect photos go straight to the fleet manager. Red, amber and green status per vehicle live on the dashboard. <a href="/pages/van-safety-check-template.html">Full template →</a></p>
            </article>
            <article id="site-reports" class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Structural</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title"><a href="/pages/structural-site-report-template.html">Site inspection reports — structural</a></h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Capture site notes, photos, sketches and measurements on WhatsApp during the visit. Structured draft report ready by the time the engineer is back at the desk. Accountable engineer reviews and signs. <a href="/pages/structural-site-report-template.html">Full template →</a></p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

